challenges.description:
What is the key runtime difference between these two?

  // CommonJS
  const fs = require('fs')
  module.exports = { readFile }

  // ESM
  import fs from 'fs'
  export function readFile() {}

You have a legacy JavaScript utility with no types:

```js
// metrics.js
function increment(name, value = 1) { /* sends metric */ }
function gauge(name, value) { /* sets gauge */ }
function timing(name, durationMs) { /* records timing */ }
module.exports = { increment, gauge, timing }
```

Write `metrics.d.ts` that declares the types for this module so TypeScript consumers get full type safety.

Include a `MetricName` type alias for string (for documentation purposes) and make all functions return void.
